<title>NORWAY: Norway Christiania, Storebrand on observation list.</title>
<headline>Norway Christiania, Storebrand on observation list.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Oslo bourse said on Wednesday that Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse ASA and insurer Storebrand ASA had been moved to the observation list following an announcement of their proposed merger.</p>
<p>When mergers or extraordinary announcements are made, bourse authorities routinely move the companies involved to the observation list where they are monitored closely for sharp movements in share price or large trades in their stock.</p>
<p>Earlier the two companies said they had agreed to join forces to become the largest financial group in Norway and the sixth largest in the Nordic region in terms of market capitalisation.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
